{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/643130-ancestry-of-forgotten-stars","id":643130,"title":"Ancestry of Forgotten Stars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-28T09:59:59-07:00","id":643130,"title":"Ancestry of Forgotten Stars","content":"That is pretty Lovecraftian,eh? So these forgotten stars, are they somehow alive or something? Are they actually giant space squid-monkey things that eat your eyeballs if you so much as look at them through a telescope. Thanks for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T17:51:59-07:00","id":643596,"title":"","content":"Mummy in general is pretty Lovecraftian, with a good number of references to the mythos scattered throughout. Ancestry is one of the more prominent of these, given that Tier 3 basically summons Nyarlathotep.<br /> <br /> For more on the disturbing nature of stars though, you should probably check out Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:15:24-07:00","id":643694,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this power pretty much summons Nyarlathotep, and then BotD adds the Black Huriyah, who are angels of non-existence that orbit dead stars. Lore of the Deceived mentions the Ochre-Masked King, a demon who needs to be sealed away every 1,000 years. Mummy on the whole is a pretty Lovrcraftian game even without these rather explicit nods, especially when you consider stuff like Nephren-Ka and the Shining Trapezohedron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:50:11-07:00","id":643839,"title":"","content":"Which book is Ancestry from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T00:09:23-07:00","id":643847,"title":"","content":"Guildhalls of the Deathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:12:39-07:00","id":644466,"title":"","content":"Mummy fiction in general lends itself well to Lovecraft anyway. In both you have sleeping ancients from times well outside of the modern era, who rise when their sanctuaries are violated to spread horror and often madness to those who seek them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T18:02:20-07:00","id":644804,"title":"","content":"Fun fact: <i>huriyah</i> is a term for the blessed virgins of heaven that await men after we die.<br /> <br /> Far and away it's my favorite Utterance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T16:53:28-07:00","id":647376,"title":"","content":"wow, knowing that makes that power so much cooler and darker. o.o ancestry of forgotten stars was always a touch disappointing to me, due to the third tier being highly combat effective, but itd be hard to pull off the ritual in time to use it as such. Some forumites suggested the true use is the question-asking aspect, but thats one bullet point out of the many combat-type ones. it also seems to me that every su-menent and their mother would need the utterance to make the combination useful. Itd be hard to gather enough mummies to make a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-31T17:16:01-07:00","id":647408,"title":"","content":"My group settled on a use for it. It's the &quot;Siege&quot; Utterance. If you need to attack LDI's super-secret, highly fortified lab, or get past the otherwise impenetrable defences erected around a Mummy while they perform Dust Beneath Feet Tier 3, or something along those lines, that's when you use it. You set up a safe distance from the base, get your meret together (bear in mind that Acolytes don't need the Utterance to help cast it and they do help by boosting the stats of the Herald), recruit one or two NPC Su-Menent who know the Utterance and owe you a favour, and then go in. Its strange movement abilities let you close in from a good distance away, so you can sit back in safety while you cast it. Then you bull your way through the enemy's defences and, when the Utterance ends, you're all standing inside the enemy's base among the ruins of their defences.<br /> <br /> I guess the main problem is finding those locations where Dust Beneath Feet Tier 1 isn't the better option...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}